            <div xml:id="d78">

                <pb facs="0184" n="108" sameAs="frus:frus1935v02/pg108"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.5531/340: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Belgium</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Morris</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Brussels</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-02-06T13:00:00+00:00">February 6, 1935—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 6—11:53 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>7. At a meeting at Belgian Foreign Office yesterday afternoon at which Sussdorff
                    and Hughes<anchor n="19" xml:id="d78-f1"/> were present as observers,
                    representatives of General Motors, Ford and Chrysler expressed satisfaction at
                    offer of reduction on automobile parts recently cabled to Belgian Embassy in
                    Washington. The three American companies which have assembly plants in Belgium
                    are in substantial accord with the Belgian Government regarding the new rates of
                    duty on parts including the labor safeguard clause. It developed at the meeting
                    that the American companies which do not have assembly plants in Belgium will
                    derive no benefit from the proposed reduction of duty on parts on account of the
                    labor safeguard clause. This fact undoubtedly lessens the importance of the
                    concessions which the Belgian Government is prepared to offer on parts.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Morris</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d78-f1" n="19" xml:id="d78-f1-content">
                <p>Thomas L. Hughes, Commercial Attaché in Belgium.</p>
